# DTF tier manifest: scan-on-proxy-alpine  (artifact-keeper 1.12.0: #4113,
# epic #4097)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream (an Alpine v3.19
# branch whose packages carry known identities). LOCAL-ONLY: the verdicts
# come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its pre-seeded
# vulnerability DB (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: before 1.12.0 an Alpine Remote (or a Virtual over one) with
# scan_on_proxy=true streamed every .apk unscanned (200, no X-AK-Scan) and
# /api/v1/formats reported alpine `accepted`; the scanner does not catalog a
# bare .apk at all. 1.12.0 checks the package's own .PKGINFO against the
# request and grades it on the release the branch names through a synthetic
# installed system: vulnerable -> 403 scan_blocked, clean -> 200 X-AK-Scan:
# clean, a package whose .PKGINFO disagrees or whose branch names no release
# -> 423 under fail_closed with no verdict row, fail_open -> pending then
# blocked; an ambiguous client path is 400.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.5. Green: an image carrying artifact-keeper#4113.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
